2. Fonts fetched at run time (not redistributed by this repository)
-------------------------------------------------------------------

When a film names a font family that is not vendored, the engine fetches it
into the local cache (~/.cache/animspark or $ANIMSPARK_HOME) from the npm
packages @fontsource/* and @chinese-fonts/* (from an installed copy, else from
jsDelivr at the version pinned in packages/engine/src/scene/font-versions.json).
Each font is under its own license, mostly SIL OFL 1.1, some Apache-2.0 or a
free-for-commercial-use statement from the author; the engine's font library
(packages/engine/src/scene/font-library.ts) records the license of every
family. Check the license of any font you ship in a finished video.


3. GeneralUser GS SoundFont (downloaded at run time)
----------------------------------------------------

@muspark/core renders sampled instruments with GeneralUser GS v2 by
S. Christian Collins. It is not part of this repository; on first use it is
downloaded from the author's GitHub repository at a pinned commit:

  https://github.com/mrbumpy409/GeneralUser-GS
  (commit 684543d5e5efaef08d02be50dcda8d552478fa60, see
   packages/muspark/src/sampled/soundfont.ts)

Its license (GeneralUser GS License v2.0) allows use without restriction for
music creation, private or commercial, including profiting from recordings made
with it, and allows use and modification in software projects. The author asks
that websites not link directly to the download files; to use a mirror, set
MUSPARK_SOUNDFONT_URL. Full text:
https://github.com/mrbumpy409/GeneralUser-GS/blob/main/documentation/LICENSE.txt


